    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0436" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2351</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-24T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 24, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2634. Your 3375, January 21.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d199-f1"/> I have been holding
                    confidential negotiations with Bernstorff which, however, have been as yet
                    without any result. I do not feel that at the present moment you can be of
                    material assistance in these negotiations. I shall not fail to advise you as
                    soon as I have anything definite for you to act upon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
